            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "dictor and response scores rather than their covariance, solved by a matrix-free higher-order power method that never forms a moment tensor. The motivation is a simple statistical observation: a node that straddles two regimes is a mixture, mixtures are non-normal, and the between-regime separation surfaces in the third-order joint moments before it dominates the second-order ones.",
            "block_bbox": [
