        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Several extensions are natural. The coskewness objective is presently available only with the dense and sparse twoblock bases; extending it to the robust and cellwise-robust bases (Serneels, 2026b,a) would combine regime discovery with outlier resistance. A plane search in  $ c t_{2} + (1 - |c|) t_{1} $ along the lines of Eriksson et al. (2009)'s §5.4.1 would relax the axis-aligned cut. Finally, higher-order objectives beyond coskewness – cokurtosis, or a joint independent-component criterion (De Lathauwer et al., 2000a) – are a natural continuation of the same programme.",
